@startuml UC-P2-manage-project-members-analysis-sequence
!include ../../domain/diagrams/_style.puml
hide footbox
title UC-P2 Manage project members (analysis: system sequence)
' Analysis level (decision 9): the person and Playground as one box. No outside system takes part.
' Split from the design because security rules shape the steps (who may change members, an administrator's
' one narrow power, the same answer for a project that is not yours).
' No route, store, port, adapter, token or cookie. Step numbers are the main flow numbers of UC-P2.
' Not drawn: the reason an administrator gives when restoring a manager (the use case keeps it in the audit
' entry, but no step asks for it), and the affected person's next request (step 9).

actor "Caller" as U
participant "Playground" as PG #E6F0FB

U -> PG : 1 open a project\nand its members
U -> PG : 2 add, change a role,\nor remove\n3 (add) the person, the role
alt caller is not in the project
  PG --> U : 4 same answer as\na missing project
else caller is an engineer
  PG --> U : 4 refused
else administrator, not a manager here
  alt adds a manager, none active,\nan active person, not themselves
    PG -> PG : 7 add the manager
    PG -> PG : 8 record, with the reason
    PG --> U : updated members
  else anything else
    PG -> PG : 8 record the attempt
    PG --> U : 4 refused
  end
else caller manages this project
  alt person to add not active
    PG --> U : 5 refused, one answer
  else no active manager would remain
    PG --> U : 6 refused
  else person to change or\nremove is not a member
    PG --> U : refused
  else
    PG -> PG : 7 apply the change
    PG -> PG : 8 record who, what, whom
    PG --> U : updated members
  end
end
@enduml
